Example: buying a fund with selected cash is an internal exchange.
The first day deposits 100 USD into Assets:Cash. On 2024-01-02 the portfolio
starts with that 100 USD of cash, then spends it on one FUND unit costing 100.
Both cash and FUND are selected, so the -100 USD cash movement and +100 USD
fund acquisition add to zero net contributions during the selected day.
The unit's closing price is 120 USD. Ending value is 120, profit/loss is
120 - 100 - 0 = 20 USD, and time-weighted return is 120 / 100 - 1 = 20%.
The money-weighted returns cannot be calculated for this one-day interval, so
the text formatter shows their null API values as n/a.

========== API ==========

investmentPerformance({ accounts: ['^Assets:'], commodities: ['USD', 'FUND'], from: '2024-01-02', to: '2024-01-02' })

========== API FORMAT ==========

text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Cash
account Assets:Fund
account Equity:Opening
P 2024-01-01 FUND 100 USD
P 2024-01-02 FUND 120 USD

2024-01-01 Deposit
  Assets:Cash  100 USD
  Equity:Opening  -100 USD

2024-01-02 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -100 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2024-01-02 to 2024-01-02
Instruments: 2
Opening value: 100.00 USD
Net contributions: 0.00 USD
Ending value: 120.00 USD
Profit/loss: 20.00 USD
Time-weighted return: 20.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): n/a
Money-weighted return (annualized): n/a

========== WARNINGS ==========
